WEBVTT

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:10.860
Saku-chan! Look at this!

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:12.240
It's the stars!

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.230
Saku-chan, you're moving away soon, right?

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.560
You should look at them while you still can.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.530
What are you talking about, Mii-chan?

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.780
All you did was take my book hostage.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.400
Now give me back my book!

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.830
You like books more than stars.

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:32.370
You're weird, Saku-chan.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:34.610
Shut up!

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:35.700
It's none of your business!

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:39.170
That reminds me, Saku-chan. Let me show you something special.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.810
It's the light from a star.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:46.650
My daddy gave it to me.

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:50.500
He asked the stars to share their light.

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:54.530
That's so obviously a toy!

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:57.400
I'll ask them to share some with you too!

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.090
W-Wait, Mii-chan!

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.530
Mii-chan, that's dangerous!

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:07.090
Don't worry. I'm fine.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:09.830
See? Just a little more...

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:14.590
Mii-chan!

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:31.750
That hurt...

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:39.860
You touched my hand when I stretched them out so far...

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:53.670
Just one word is fine.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.520
Just voice your dreams.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:00.640
It's your first step and first sign to realization.

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:04.750
Ask yourself what is it that you like?

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.880
Your answers will...

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:11.860
blow your questions high into the sky.

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:08.290
Even more...

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.180
Like fireworks...

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:18.390
Even though we should all try to be more honest we ourselves, we can't.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:25.390
Maybe I should try summoning my soul as a child?

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:31.920
What touched my hand when i stretched them out so far...

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:37.070
was a Supernova that suddenly appear to this new night.

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:43.030
For millions of light years, it never stops inside of me.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:51.250
The longer I gaze, the more power my eyes absorb...

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:56.510
and that's because... because I'm a star too!

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:14.850
Good morning, Saku.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:16.100
Did you sleep well?

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:20.500
Oh my, why does your face look like a squashed cockroach?

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:21.060
C-Cockroach-

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:23.800
You fell asleep while reading a book again, didn't you?

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:27.040
Is that something you should even be saying to your son?

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:32.240
Well, this is all thanks to your dad agreeing to work and live on his own,

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:35.140
so that you can spend your high school years in the city you've missed.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:36.180
Yes, yes.

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:37.720
Of course I'm grateful for that.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:41.780
Really? Then why don't you look happier?

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:44.610
But why does it have to be <i>this</i> city?

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.590
What's this?! You've already tied your tie?!

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:48.950
What-

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:50.410
What happened to letting Mom have some fun?!

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:51.500
What happened to letting Mom have some fun?!

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:52.250
Like I care!

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:56.060
You do everything so promptly.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:57.350
Mommy's so sad now.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:00.880
Well then, I'm off.

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:03.230
Wait!

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:03.970
Pictures!

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.870
You already took a ton of them at my entrance ceremony!

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:10.090
Saku, this way...

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:11.510
Good boy.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:12.260
She's...

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:13.690
That reminds me,

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:17.160
I wonder how she's doing.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:19.220
You know, the girl who is a year older than you, Mii-chan.

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:20.650
She used to live in the apartment above us.

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:25.700
I haven't really mentioned her because it used to always put you in such a bad mood,

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.130
but Mii-chan-

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:30.420
Like I care!

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:33.640
My! He's at the rebellious age!

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:39.010
I've finally returned to this city where I lived for two years after we moved here in first grade.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:43.680
It's a moderately developed suburb-an average city.

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:49.360
However, a devil once lived in this city...

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:51.470
Mii-chan...

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:52.830
Mihoshi.

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:55.030
Back then, she was the embodiment of fear.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:56.590
The silent invader.

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.430
Having moved into an apartment complex with few children...

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:04.840
during my first grade, I was the perfect prey for Mii-chan.

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:10.510
Thanks to her, the times when I was relaxing were continuously interrupted,

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:09.790
Saku-chan, let's play.

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:14.070
and I'd spend days being introduced to new games and being lost in the wild.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:17.670
Where am I?

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:22.270
Just my luck, her father loved the stars,

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:25.290
so she used to drag me around day and night.

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:27.170
And then-

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:41.930
O' Lord, why must I spend my high school years in the city I dread the most?

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:46.960
However, it's been seven years since then.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:49.770
She should be a high schooler as well.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:54.480
She might have turned into a female Gian and is no longer interested in the stars.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:54.460
[Note: Gian is a bully from the series "Doraemon."]

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:58.860
As time passes, the people, and even the city, change.

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:05.230
Even the tall, scary "ghost tree" no longer exists.

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:10.940
What is this?

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:13.910
These are...

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:21.340
Stars in broad daylight?

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:26.530
Hello, boys and girls!

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:28.880
Do you like stars?!

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:35.870
The Astronomy Club is currently looking for lots and lots of new members!

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:40.380
Let's watch the stars together, everyone!

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:44.480
That's...

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:50.690
What are you doing, Mihoshi?!

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:52.120
M-M-M-Mihoshi-kun-

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:56.520
What will the Student Council say if they find out we're running such a flashy recruitment drive?!

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:57.310
She's right, you know.

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:59.710
We've only just founded the club too!

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:00.890
Mihoshi...

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:04.310
M-Mii-chan?!

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:07.710
Oh, shit!

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:22.060
This is bad!

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:23.400
This is definitely bad!

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:26.880
Saku-chan?

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:32.210
This is bad!

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:33.140
This is bad!

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:35.040
What the hell's up with her?

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:37.420
She hasn't changed at all!

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:46.210
Saku-chan!

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:48.300
Saku-chan!

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:50.390
It really <i>is</i> you!

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:51.130
Why?

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:52.130
Why are you here?

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:54.810
It's a mistake. You're mistaking me for someone else!

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:55.530
Liar.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:57.010
You're definitely Saku-chan.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:59.590
You called me Mii-chan, after all.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:00.660
I did not!

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:03.600
Besides, with that Ghibli hairstyle of yours, there's no mistaking it. It's definitely you!

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:04.390
[Note: Most of the male characters in Studio Ghibli movies share a common hairstyle.]

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:04.440
What?!

00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:05.670
What kind of reasoning is that?!

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:07.040
Saku-chan, wait!

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:09.080
I'm telling you, you're mistaken!

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:10.240
Then why are you running away from me?!

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:11.330
Saku-chan!

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:12.880
Saku-chan!

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:27.560
Saku-chan...

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:30.990
Saku-chan!

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:30.990
Someone, save me!

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:32.320
Save me!

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:34.070
Hey, Mihoshi!

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:36.200
Sayo-chin! President!

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.790
Don't straddle people!

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:38.600
Behave yourself!

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:44.510
U-Um... are you okay?

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:48.320
Y-You're a life saver.

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:49.550
I'm sorry.

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:52.330
She's rather uncontrollable when she gets enthusiastic.

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:57.610
More importantly, do you two know each other?

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:00.040
Yup!

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:00.020
No.

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:04.180
Why?!

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:05.700
I don't quite understand the situation, but...

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:08.240
I'm Yarai Sayo from the Astronomy Club.

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:10.190
And I'm the President, Roma.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:10.600
I know!

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:12.590
Would you like to join our club?

00:09:13.090 --> 00:09:15.750
To be honest, we only founded the club recently, so we lack members.

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:18.560
Sayo-chin, that's a brilliant idea!

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:21.070
She's right! You should join the Astronomy Club.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:22.950
Saku-chan, you like stars, right?

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:25.700
If you do, we can look at the stars together again.

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:27.980
N-No, I...

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:30.200
Hey, Astronomy Club!

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:32.700
What was all that ruckus?!

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:35.460
I'll remove your right to use the rooftop!

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:36.440
She's here.

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:37.690
It's the Student Council President.

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:40.320
Come on, Mihoshi, we're going.

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:41.700
Saku-chan!

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:44.100
I will definitely bring this up at the Student Council meeting!

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:52.640
Calm down...

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:54.050
Calm down, Saku.

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:55.930
All I need to do is avoid her.

00:09:56.630 --> 00:10:00.220
I can spend my high school days in peace as long as I avoid her.

00:10:05.780 --> 00:10:06.660
Hey, did you see it?

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:07.970
You mean the incident earlier?

00:10:08.350 --> 00:10:11.700
I heard a senior straddled a freshman!

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:14.570
Not only that, it was a female senior on top of a male freshman!

00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:15.190
Say,

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:17.420
can I talk to you?

00:10:17.790 --> 00:10:19.960
All you've done so far is read your book.

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:22.340
S-Sure...

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:24.100
Thank goodness!

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:27.160
There isn't anyone in this class who went to the same middle school as me.

00:10:27.590 --> 00:10:30.290
I'm Edogawa. Nice to meet you.

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:32.470
You were... Ooyagi, right?

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:34.300
Which middle school did you go to?

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:36.610
I'm not from around here.

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:38.750
I lived in Fukuoka before coming here.

00:10:38.810 --> 00:10:39.520
Really?

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:41.900
Um.... Fukuoka...

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:42.920
I see...

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:45.750
Hey, what's that?

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:47.090
What? What is it?

00:10:47.340 --> 00:10:48.620
Look at the class over on the other side.

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:49.650
What is she doing?

00:10:52.340 --> 00:10:53.940
What's with that senior?

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:55.510
She's staring at us!

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:57.290
Stop it, Mii-chan...

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:03.580
Saku-chan!

00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:04.880
I'm here to visit you!

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:09.980
What? He's not here?!

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:11.840
He left the moment the bell rang?!

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:12.860
Good...

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:15.640
Just try not to be seen...

00:11:15.770 --> 00:11:19.540
Hey, isn't she the girl who straddled that male freshman?

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:21.880
What? What do you mean?

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:24.340
What exactly is Ooyagi-kun to her?

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:26.120
The position I've been aiming for...

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:28.790
To not stand out too much or be underestimated...

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:33.930
What? He's gone again?

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:39.100
Again?

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:44.220
He left the moment the bell rang.

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:50.050
Hey, Mihoshi!

00:11:58.480 --> 00:11:59.730
I can finally relax...

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:06.180
If I wait it out here, I'm sure Mii-chan-I mean, Mihoshi will give up.

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:12.150
Saku-chan, Saku-chan, Saku-chan, Saku-chan, Saku-chan...

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:14.120
Mii-chan!

00:12:15.570 --> 00:12:16.610
I'm sorry!

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:19.630
W-What do you think you're doing?!

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:22.050
Well, you're never around when I visit your classroom, so...

00:12:22.210 --> 00:12:23.320
Still-

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:26.990
But I finally caught up with you.

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:31.570
Say, do you remember this?

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:33.290
I still wear it.

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:34.900
Why?

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:39.140
Do you remember me telling you that I made the stars share their light with it?

00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:39.090
Why are you acting so normally?

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:40.570
I-

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:43.020
Whatever, I don't remember.

00:12:43.390 --> 00:12:43.600
What?

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:47.370
It's not like I returned to this city because I wanted to.

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:49.380
This is a real pain.

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:52.240
Can you please look for new members elsewhere?

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:53.800
What?

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:55.250
Good bye.

00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:05.500
No...

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:06.990
No...

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:08.970
No!

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:13.290
Mihoshi?

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:14.630
Why?!

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:15.930
Why, Saku-chan?!

00:13:16.240 --> 00:13:17.930
When we finally manage to see each other again!

00:13:18.220 --> 00:13:19.230
Please remember it...

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:22.610
When we ran down that path at night, chasing after the moon.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:25.650
When we reached out to catch the star's light.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:29.660
They're all precious memories.

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:31.380
Saku-chan...

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:35.240
What...

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:37.800
...part of that was?!

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:40.790
Precious memories?!

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:42.000
What the hell is that?!

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:46.020
I wasn't going to mention this, but let me tell you this!

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:47.990
This is the truth!

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:51.460
Saku-chan, if we run after it, we might be able to see the other side of the moon.

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:53.570
Do you know just how painful that was for me?!

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:54.680
Saku-chan, we might be able to catch the stars!

00:13:55.050 --> 00:13:58.150
My classmates teased me because I always played with girls,

00:13:58.460 --> 00:14:00.210
and when I was reading, I was always interrupted!

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:02.790
Every, every, every single time!

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:08.640
All you did was drag around a quiet indoor-type boy who loves to read books!

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:14.330
What's more, you always dragged me around,

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:18.780
but when I broke my arm, was released from the hospital, and was about to move away from the city,

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:21.180
you didn't even come and see me off.

00:14:24.350 --> 00:14:25.080
That's...

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:27.700
That's my...

00:14:28.230 --> 00:14:29.860
That's my line.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:33.580
When I left the hospital, you were already gone.

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:35.590
I couldn't even say good bye.

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:39.510
I-I've always wanted to see you again.

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:42.850
Now that you mention it, Mihoshi,

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:46.220
you were hospitalized after falling out of a tree back in elementary school.

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:47.380
What?

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:52.610
I haven't really mentioned her because it always used to put you in such a bad mood...

00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:56.040
Saku, Mii-chan is actually-

00:14:56.510 --> 00:14:57.050
I don't want to hear it.

00:14:57.520 --> 00:14:58.960
Don't talk about Mii-chan.

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:05.580
What? Was I just lonely?

00:15:08.690 --> 00:15:09.090
I'm sorry.

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:10.310
What?

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:13.350
I'm sorry. Forgive me.

00:15:14.070 --> 00:15:15.030
Saku-chan?

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:18.130
Does that mean you remember me?

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:18.820
Yes...

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:20.260
So, I'm not a pain?

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:20.780
Yes...

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:22.670
You've remembered our past together?

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:23.300
Yes...

00:15:23.590 --> 00:15:25.590
So, will you join the Astronomy Club too?

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:27.500
Yes, so hurry up and stop crying, okay?

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:32.410
Okay!

00:15:34.610 --> 00:15:37.330
And stop hugging me all the time!

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:44.400
Hello!

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:47.760
This room is somehow...

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:50.360
It still contains things from when this was the Earth Science Club room.

00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:56.620
The Earth Science Club studied all the natural sciences of the universe, so we could have left it as that.

00:15:57.010 --> 00:15:59.160
But we don't have any earth science classes,

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:01.450
so no one joined.

00:16:01.970 --> 00:16:06.910
So when all the third-year members graduated, Mihoshi suggested we change it to the Astronomy Club.

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:09.540
We've got tatami mattresses too!

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:10.830
Aren't they great?

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:12.100
Oh?

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:16.040
Although, it's kind of a pity; it was fun studying things other than astronomy.

00:16:16.630 --> 00:16:17.990
Like collecting rocks, right?

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:20.330
Let's do that again when we get funding.

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:21.660
That's...

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:26.400
So, what's this out-of-place futon doing in this room then?

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:28.890
Why that's for sleeping in, of course!

00:16:29.640 --> 00:16:31.990
We cuddle up in it when we're watching the stars.

00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:32.520
Seriously?

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:34.670
Is that how it is?

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:37.600
I've never actively participated in any club activities.

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:45.280
Mornin', President!

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:46.530
Hi.

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:49.750
I felt a little dizzy, so I was resting.

00:16:50.930 --> 00:16:52.760
Don't scare me like that!

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:55.160
Oh! You're the boy from this morning.

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:57.790
I'm Ooyagi Saku.

00:16:58.580 --> 00:16:59.760
Pleased to meet you.

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:04.030
Oh! You did well, Mihoshi-kun, Yarai-kun.

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:04.800
Yup.

00:17:05.140 --> 00:17:06.630
One more and that'll make five.

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:07.650
All right!

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:09.510
Let's do our best with the recruitment drive!

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:11.920
I have a feeling we'll be getting some new members!

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:12.430
What?

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:16.330
Even if you join, we're still short on members.

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:20.610
We're newly formed, so they're treating us as a club for the time being.

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:23.900
But if we don't have a minimum of five people, we have to disband or form a friendly gathering instead.

00:17:35.480 --> 00:17:37.680
It sure is club recruitment week.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:39.560
All the clubs are working so hard.

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:47.750
I-I think we're a little... inconspicuous...

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:51.050
We don't have a uniform like the sports clubs do.

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:54.020
Well, guess we have no choice but to pass out fliers...

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:57.310
A uniform!

00:17:57.310 --> 00:17:58.780
Think of it as a uniform!

00:17:58.810 --> 00:17:59.890
No, I can't!

00:18:00.310 --> 00:18:01.910
Come on, Sayo-chin, you too!

00:18:02.250 --> 00:18:04.020
Stop it, Mihoshi.

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:05.860
Geez... Sayo-chin!

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:09.160
Okay, as the club's President, it's time for me-

00:18:09.470 --> 00:18:10.430
President Roma!

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:14.760
President, you shouldn't force yourself!

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:15.980
President!

00:18:16.340 --> 00:18:19.040
Oh my, so it's true that you've managed to find yourself a new member.

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:23.580
Student Council President!

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:23.510
Fumin!

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:26.750
And <i>who</i> are you calling Fumin?

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:29.380
Well, whatever.

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:31.170
Anyway, don't forget.

00:18:31.740 --> 00:18:33.280
You only have until the end of this month.

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:35.550
If you don't get five members by then, you're just a friendly gathering.

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:37.290
You won't qualify for any finances.

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:38.860
I know that!

00:18:39.030 --> 00:18:40.350
Fumin, you meanie!

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:46.680
I will never acknowledge a stupid club that gives estimated expenses of 200,000 or 300,000 yen!

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:48.600
P-President, calm down.

00:18:48.650 --> 00:18:49.570
Shut up, Haraguchi.

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:52.050
But it <i>is</i> that expensive! We need telescopes and stuff like that!

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:53.750
I'm just telling you to choose something cheaper.

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:56.550
You can find something for like 10,000 yen.

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:57.030
They're fighting, just like always...

00:18:57.360 --> 00:18:58.600
Kotodzuka Fumie.

00:18:58.930 --> 00:19:00.890
She went to the same elementary and middle school as us.

00:19:01.090 --> 00:19:03.220
She always seems to pick fights with us.

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:06.300
With such a racket, no one can join the club even if they wanted to.

00:19:08.050 --> 00:19:09.390
Are you their newest member?

00:19:09.890 --> 00:19:10.990
Yes...

00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:13.010
Haraguchi, note it down.

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:13.850
Okay.

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:15.320
"Akeno's boyfriend."

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:16.500
No, I'm not!

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:19.060
So? What's your name?

00:19:19.620 --> 00:19:20.880
It's Ooyagi Saku.

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:26.700
It's spelled using the characters "big," "eight," and "tree." Saku is spelled as in "Saku" for Hagiwara Sakutarou.

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:29.120
Hagi... Sakutarou?

00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:31.170
Yes.

00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:32.780
My parents were big fans of his.

00:19:34.470 --> 00:19:36.010
The L-Literature Club?!

00:19:36.490 --> 00:19:39.140
President Kotodzuka, you're a member of the Literature Club?

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:41.480
Y-Yes, I am.

00:19:43.940 --> 00:19:45.570
No!

00:19:45.860 --> 00:19:48.250
Emergency!

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:52.420
That was close.

00:19:52.630 --> 00:19:54.040
That was too close, Saku-chan.

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:58.070
I-I just wanted to read a few books...

00:19:58.330 --> 00:19:59.470
Even though you say that,

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:03.010
you're probably secretly thinking that it doesn't matter if we don't manage to form this club, aren't you?

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:05.010
Hey!

00:20:05.110 --> 00:20:06.390
You can't blame me for that!

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:09.310
I haven't done any stargazing since I left the city.

00:20:09.970 --> 00:20:13.690
Besides, even a friendly gathering of people can stargaze together,

00:20:14.030 --> 00:20:16.270
so I don't think it's necessary to form a club.

00:20:18.520 --> 00:20:22.160
But then it'll just be us enjoying ourselves.

00:20:24.960 --> 00:20:28.230
You know, I want everyone to see...

00:20:28.690 --> 00:20:30.500
...the sky that moved me.

00:20:31.050 --> 00:20:32.270
And I really want to share my memories with everyone.

00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:36.760
The stars that my dad first showed me when I was small.

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:41.970
The Milky Way that was spread out before my eyes was surprisingly huge,

00:20:42.490 --> 00:20:45.300
and as I stood still, I felt like I was going to be sucked in.

00:20:46.190 --> 00:20:47.280
The sensations I felt back then...

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:48.520
The excitement I felt back then...

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:52.420
...can only be understood by someone who's looked up and reached out.

00:20:53.170 --> 00:20:54.340
A memory anyone in this world can make.

00:20:54.980 --> 00:20:57.000
A quiet and vast one...

00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:00.170
That's why I want everyone to experience it too.

00:21:00.890 --> 00:21:03.620
Forever... I want it to last beyond our graduation.

00:21:04.390 --> 00:21:05.200
Forever...

00:21:05.770 --> 00:21:07.860
And to achieve that, the first generation of the Astronomy Club needs to work hard!

00:21:08.310 --> 00:21:09.940
And that means us.

00:21:10.260 --> 00:21:11.230
Maybe that was a little cheesy...

00:21:13.780 --> 00:21:14.860
Mii-chan...

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:17.990
I know!

00:21:18.390 --> 00:21:19.250
I've got an idea!

00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:24.250
There's something the Astronomy Club can do in broad daylight too!

00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:25.510
M-Mihoshi?

00:21:26.060 --> 00:21:28.750
The Sunspot Observation!

00:21:29.610 --> 00:21:30.310
Sun?

00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:31.360
That's right.

00:21:31.420 --> 00:21:33.120
It's one of our few gadgets.

00:21:33.470 --> 00:21:35.960
We project the sun onto a background using a pair of binoculars.

00:21:36.530 --> 00:21:38.520
It's something more than one person can observe.

00:21:39.050 --> 00:21:39.920
You're amazing.

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:41.310
Let's hurry, Saku-chan.

00:21:42.460 --> 00:21:44.000
Sayo-chin! President!

00:21:45.540 --> 00:21:47.150
Mihoshi, it's raining.

00:21:50.140 --> 00:21:51.390
How ironic.

00:21:52.390 --> 00:21:56.830
As I look out, I get the feeling that more people look up at the sky when it's raining.

00:21:57.490 --> 00:21:59.080
Maybe it's just my imagination.

00:21:59.440 --> 00:22:00.000
No, it's not.

00:22:00.780 --> 00:22:01.480
But more importantly...

00:22:02.040 --> 00:22:05.130
Oh my, the sunspots are very clear today.

00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:07.400
Cut it out already!

00:22:07.820 --> 00:22:09.410
But!

00:22:09.410 --> 00:22:12.500
What if it rains tomorrow as well?

00:22:11.270 --> 00:22:11.950
Geez...

00:22:12.580 --> 00:22:14.010
Sayo-chin!

00:22:14.490 --> 00:22:16.240
Saku-chan, where are you going?

00:22:17.190 --> 00:22:17.890
The library.

00:22:18.090 --> 00:22:18.770
The libr-?!

00:22:18.910 --> 00:22:20.180
I knew it!

00:22:20.220 --> 00:22:23.080
Saku-chan prefers books and the Literature Club, after all!

00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:24.150
No, I don't!

00:22:26.220 --> 00:22:30.350
If I blow up some astronomy photos and post them up, it'll attract more attention.

00:22:31.030 --> 00:22:32.320
I'm going to the library to borrow some.

00:22:35.240 --> 00:22:36.290
W-What is it?

00:22:36.880 --> 00:22:38.870
Saku-chan, I love you!

00:22:38.910 --> 00:22:39.990
Stop it!

00:22:39.850 --> 00:22:44.200
I look up at the sky, and I think of you…

00:22:41.640 --> 00:22:42.640
President!

00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:47.880
but I can’t find the words,

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:48.640
We ended up staying rather late, didn't we?

00:22:48.840 --> 00:22:49.370
Thanks to you,

00:22:49.020 --> 00:22:51.180
I want to tell you,

00:22:49.390 --> 00:22:50.870
we were able to make some wonderful display props.

00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:52.770
Tomorrow we'll get some new members for sure.

00:22:51.180 --> 00:22:53.700
but they just slip away…

00:22:52.910 --> 00:22:54.430
Look! The sky's cleared up!

00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:57.370
almost like Shooting Stars.

00:22:57.860 --> 00:23:01.950
In this Wave of Silence,

00:23:02.330 --> 00:23:06.320
a ray of light flickers the darkness

00:23:06.790 --> 00:23:11.630
playing with my memories

00:23:11.630 --> 00:23:17.470
and releasing my heart.

00:23:18.300 --> 00:23:20.410
Into the future,

00:23:20.410 --> 00:23:28.980
I will have these feelings again!

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:33.390
No worries, I’m not alone.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:35.240
I think this is the first time I've gazed at the stars since that day.

00:23:34.650 --> 00:23:39.590
You have taught me I’m not alone.

00:23:37.150 --> 00:23:38.320
Saku-chan, welcome back.

00:23:39.050 --> 00:23:41.720
And welcome to the Astronomy Club!

00:25:17.520 --> 00:25:27.530
Rival of Love???

00:25:17.520 --> 00:25:27.530
Makita Hime Appears!!
